From 1551dccc87a4b5eccc8c12ec9080a5cbb6012114 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: allcodernet <67543055+allcodernet@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 25 Sep 2026 21:41:41 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 22/45] decide-trie: full-path plan, vocabulary indexes,
 context tries

decide-vocab: ends_value is the value-end predicate of spec 4.1;
build_vocab_index builds END and MERGED over the pieces of every
non-control token (MERGED[b] holds the tokens whose piece is b + r
with ends(r)).

build_tries takes a scoring_mode. Full-path mode keeps the joint
tokenisation and the distinct-path check but skips the sibling check
and the quote-split fallback (spec 4.2), so "sale"/"sales" builds; it
lists in field_trie.resplit the options whose tokens before the last
one change when ",\n" follows (spec 4.8). trie_set records the mode,
and branches_per_state is B of spec 4.3 (the option count in
full-path mode). field_trie gains option_nodes (root to leaf).

full_path_plan gives one sequence per option (stem + path) and the
token indices whose rows are read; each node is read once, in the
first option whose path holds it. context_trie tokenises lines +
stem_text + encoded jointly per option, takes the common prefix as the
stem and requires the lines-free paths (500 engine naming the field
otherwise); a quote-split trie keeps its rule (stem = lines +
stem_text + "\""). resplit is the spec 4.8 comparison.

decide-api passes the mode from options.scoring; the full-path guard
still stops full-path requests before the engine, which stays on tree.

test-decide-trie: ends_value table and resplit cases (no model), END
and MERGED["\""] (printed), full-path sale/sales, plan coverage,
context tries for score, bool, choice and quote-split fields over
three lines texts (one with a token across the lines/key boundary),
and a printed re-split survey of candidate keys (none re-split on
Qwen2.5 or Gemma 4).
